'''Scorch''' is an Elemental [[Ailment]] associated with [[fire]] that causes the affected target to have their [[Resistance|Elemental Resistances]] lowered by up to 30%, based on the Fire Damage of the Hit, for 4 seconds.

==Mechanics==
Scorch's magnitude is given by the formula: 

{{math|formula=
E = 1/2 * ({D \over T})^{0.4} * (1 + M)
}}

where D is the fire damage dealt, T is the enemy's ailment threshold, and M is the sum of the attacker's increases to the effect of scorch/non-damaging ailments (normally 0%).<ref name="Q&AMay2021"/> Usually the ailment threshold is equal to the monster's full life, except some end-game bosses such as [[The Shaper]]. To achieve the maximum magnitude , the player character needed to deal damage equal to (0.6^2.5)*100% of the ailment threshold, which roughly equal to 28% of the ailment threshold, or 28% life for most monsters. These calculations do not account for increases to ailment effect.

Scorched with a base effect lower than 2% is discarded. Scorched inflicted through means other than hit damage has a base effect of 10%. 
