==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.21.1|
* Elemental Ailments other than Freeze are no longer discarded if their duration is lower than 300ms.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.0|
* Scorch and Brittle (alternate ailments for Fire and Cold damage respectively) have both had their maximum effects raised. Scorch reduces elemental resistances by a maximum of 30% (from 20%). Brittle now increases the chance to critically strike an afflicted enemy by up to 15% (from 10%). Scorch, Brittle and Sap now all have a base duration of 4 seconds (from 2).
}}
{{Version history table row|3.9.0|
* We've added an Ailment Threshold to monsters. In the great majority of cases, the Ailment Threshold matches the monster's Maximum Life. It primarily differs for especially high-life monsters (such as The Shaper), where the threshold is reduced to allow ailments to be applied with hits that wouldn't ordinarily reach the required Life thresholds.
* The alternate ailments Sap, '''Scorch''' and Brittle have a slightly different calculation as they have lower caps on their magnitudes.<ref name="Q&AMay2021"/>
}}
{{Version history table row|3.5.0|
* Introduced to the game.
* Updated the reminder text for Ailments to include the '''3 new Ailments'''.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

